[{"id":4059222537,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7x8tIJ","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I looked at this with the animation team and we are happy with the UI in terms of the animation editor.\n\nAs for the GUI code, ResizableScrollBar has some missing code for vertical scroll and it's not properly exposed and documented as GDClass.\nThe main issue is that we have unreviewed gui code being added to the Godot runtime, even though it is not public and only used in the editor. I looked at the code and I think it is good, but the gui team would need to take a look at it.\n\nI see two ways forward for this PR.\n\n1. We keep this just as an animation editor-specific change. We keep what you have for animation track editor, since it looks really good for this purpose, and move resizable_scroll_bar.cpp to the editor directory (or editor/animation), since it is not exposed and only used in the editor. Later, someone else can expose it to the gui when the time comes.\n2. Or, if you have more time, do a few finishing touches, implement the missing cases for vertical scrolling, add documentation, and put it on the agenda for a gui meeting so the gui team can give feedback, and expose it as an official Godot GUI class.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#pullrequestreview-4059222537","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114289","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114289#pullrequestreview-4059222537"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114289"}},"submitted_at":"2026-04-05T07:23:47Z","commit_id":null},{"id":4946425679,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJtR3Tw","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested this PR and it looks good from a usability standpoint – aside from 1 nitpick which I suspect may not even be fixable.\n\nDidn't look at the code, so it still needs a GUI team review.\n\nThe nitpick: when you are zoomed out past what the handle bar can logically represent (120% of the animation length, it seems), it jumps the zoom back to 